@page "/research"
@using PullbackStrategyLab.Web.Shell
@model ResearchModel
@*
    The research ledger. Four sections, in the order the loop runs: what has been registered,
    what each version has accumulated, what the budget has left, and the twin-pair panel that
    arrives with the finder that fills it.

    Designed from ARCHITECTURE's description rather than from a drawing. SCREENS.html drew this
    page and was retired at 4.12 once the other four screens existed, so what remains is the
    specification rather than the picture, which is the right way round.

    Two rules are visible in the shape. A version's sides are separate blocks and there is no
    element on this page that could hold one number over both. And nothing here averages a
    difference series: settling a version against its target is AcceptanceGate's at 6.7, and a
    page that did it first would be answering that question with no gate in front of it.
*@
<h1>@Model.Item.Title</h1>
<p class="lede">@Model.Item.What.</p>

<p class="muted">As of @Model.Research.AsOf.</p>

<section class="ledger register">
    <h2>The register of rule versions</h2>
    <p class="muted">
        Every version, live and closed alike. A version that misses its target closes as refuted
        and stays here rather than quietly vanishing, which is the whole reason this is a register
        and not a list of what is currently running.
    </p>

    @if (!Model.Research.HasVersions)
    {
        @* "Nothing registered yet" and "this page is not built" are different facts and the words
           have to be different too. Every unbuilt screen in this shell says "Nothing here yet", so
           a built page reusing that sentence would report itself as unbuilt on the one surface a
           person reads. *@
        <div class="empty-state">
            <p><b>No version registered.</b> @Model.Research.Absent.</p>
            <p>The screen is built and the register is empty. The lab flags, records and measures
               setups with no version existing at all; what it cannot do until one is registered is
               publish a plan or difference anything against a baseline.</p>
        </div>
    }
    else
    {
        <p class="lede">Generation @Model.Research.Generation is in force.</p>

        void Versions(string heading, string note, IReadOnlyList<VersionView> versions)
        {
            if (versions.Count == 0)
            {
                return;
            }

            <h3>@heading <span class="pill">@versions.Count</span></h3>
            <p class="muted">@note</p>

            <table class="ledger versions">
                <tr>
                    <th>Version</th><th>Family</th><th>What it changes</th>
                    <th>Target</th><th>Minimum sample</th><th>Status</th><th>Registered</th>
                    <th>Age</th>
                </tr>
                @foreach (VersionView version in versions)
                {
                    <tr class="@(version.Open ? null : "resolved")">
                        <td>@version.VariantId</td>
                        <td>@version.Family</td>
                        <td>
                            @version.Definition
                            @if (version.Moved is string moved)
                            {
                                @* The five columns the store holds together, said as one line.
                                   A version differs from the baseline by exactly one gate's
                                   threshold, and this is that threshold. *@
                                <span class="moved">@moved</span>
                            }
                        </td>
                        <td>@version.Target</td>
                        @* The unit travels with the figure, because 1802 effective observations
                           and 200 rows are not comparable and one integer with no unit would
                           make them look it. *@
                        <td>@version.Sample</td>
                        <td>@version.StatusReads</td>
                        <td>@version.CreatedAt</td>
                        @* The failure table's own clause: a version whose sample never accumulates
                           stays open and the ledger shows its age. On every row rather than on the
                           open ones, because a resolved version's age is how long it took. *@
                        <td class="age">@version.Age</td>
                    </tr>
                }
            </table>
        }

        Versions("Live", "The generation in force, which is what tonight fans a plan out to.", Model.Research.Live);
        Versions(
            "Earlier generations",
            "Still readable and no longer fanned out to. A version closed as unresolved was never "
            + "measured, because the baseline it was being compared against was edited; a rejected "
            + "one was measured and fell short. Both are history and only one of them is a finding.",
            Model.Research.EarlierGenerations);
    }
</section>

<section class="ledger differences">
    <h2>What each version has accumulated</h2>
    <p class="muted">
        One block a side. <b>The two are never added:</b> a version that helps the long side while
        hurting the short would read as no difference at all once they were, and short results carry
        a borrow assumption long results do not.
    </p>

    @if (Model.Research.LastScoreRun is ScoreRunView run)
    {
        @* Which kind of nothing a version showing no difference is. A night that found no version to
           difference and a night on which the scorer never ran read identically off the score rows
           alone, which is the shape this corpus keeps finding one level up. *@
        <p class="muted">
            The scorer last ran for the session of @run.SessionDate and ended @run.Outcome:
            @run.VersionsScored of @run.VersionsLive live version(s) carry a difference,
            over @run.NightsScored night(s) scored with @run.NightsWaiting still inside their horizon.
            @if (run.StoppedBecause is string stopped)
            {
                <span class="withheld-because">@stopped</span>
            }
        </p>
    }
    else
    {
        <p class="muted">
            <b>The scorer has never run.</b> That is a different fact from a version having no
            difference to show, and it is the one a green build cannot tell you: nothing in the
            verification harness reads the running lab.
        </p>
    }

    @* Every registered version and not only the ones carrying a scored night. **The reading is
       what says a version has no scored night**, so a loop over versions with sides would drop it
       on exactly the versions it is about: a version registered inside the scoring horizon, and a
       baseline, which has no series at all and never will. That is the sixth failure shape, where
       the store holds the right answer and the surface does not carry it. *@
    @foreach (VersionView version in Model.Research.Versions)
    {
        <h3>@version.VariantId <span class="pill">@version.Age</span></h3>

        @if (version.NoAccumulatedSample is string noSample)
        {
            @* A version the gate has not read yet is a different fact from one whose
               sample is not accumulating, and saying which is better than a blank. *@
            <p class="withheld-because">@noSample</p>
        }

        @if (version.NotSettleable is string notSettleable)
        {
            <p class="withheld-because">@notSettleable</p>
        }

        @if (version.Acceptance is AcceptanceView acceptance)
        {
            @* What the gate last read, in the two units it is read in: the accumulated
               figure against the pre-registered bar, and the age beside it. Nothing here
               is computed by the page; the figures are the reading's own. *@
            <div class="acceptance @acceptance.Verdict">
                <p class="accumulated">@acceptance.Accumulated</p>
                <p class="over">@acceptance.Population</p>
                <p class="nights">@acceptance.Nights</p>

                @if (acceptance.Interval is string interval)
                {
                    <p class="figure">@interval</p>
                }

                @if (acceptance.WinRates is string rates)
                {
                    @* Reported beside expectancy and never settled on. A version raising
                       win rate while lowering expectancy is rejected under its own name. *@
                    <p class="diagnostic">win rate, a diagnostic and never the settlement:
                        @rates</p>
                }

                <p class="withheld-because">@acceptance.Because</p>
                <p class="muted">read on @acceptance.ReadOn, @acceptance.AgeDays day(s) after
                    registration</p>
            </div>
        }

        @if (version.Sides.Count == 0)
        {
            <p class="muted">
                No night has been scored for this version, so there is no difference series here.
                A version is scored on the nights it was live on whose scoring horizon has closed,
                and a version registered inside that horizon has none yet.
            </p>
        }

        @foreach (SideView side in version.Sides)
        {
            <div class="ledger side @side.Direction">
                <h4>@side.Direction</h4>
                <p class="count">@side.Count</p>
                <p class="over">@side.Over</p>


                @if (side.Unscoreable > 0)
                {
                    <p class="warns">
                        @side.Unscoreable setup(s) whose moved gate the frozen signals could not
                        judge, counted rather than dropped: a night scored over nine of eleven names
                        is a different fact from a night scored over eleven.
                    </p>
                }

                <table class="ledger nights">
                    <tr>
                        <th>Session</th><th>Flagged</th><th>Baseline</th><th>Version</th>
                        <th>Both</th><th>Difference</th>
                    </tr>
                    @foreach (ScoredNightView night in side.Nights)
                    {
                        <tr class="@(night.Withheld ? "withheld" : null)">
                            <td>@night.SessionDate</td>
                            <td>@night.Flagged</td>
                            <td>@night.BaselineSelected</td>
                            <td>@night.VariantSelected</td>
                            <td>@night.BothSelected</td>
                            <td>
                                @if (night.MeanDifference is string difference)
                                {
                                    <span class="figure">@difference</span>
                                }
                                else
                                {
                                    <span class="figure muted">withheld</span>
                                    <span class="withheld-because">@night.WithheldBecause</span>
                                }
                            </td>
                        </tr>
                    }
                </table>
            </div>
        }

        <p class="muted">
            <b>The series and not a mean of it.</b> The mean, the interval and the verdict above are
            AcceptanceGate's own reading, read back from the store rather than computed here, against
            the minimum sample written at creation and never since. A running average computed by
            this page would be that answer computed twice, with the page as the last place anybody
            looked.
        </p>
    }
</section>

<section class="ledger holdout">
    <h2>The holdout budget</h2>
    <p class="muted">
        Quarters of forward-collected evidence, non-overlapping, capped at eight. One is spent per
        decision between context-pack versions and never reused for any purpose. The register is
        created empty and a window becomes available the day its quarter completes, so it fills up
        over two years rather than starting full.
    </p>

    <dl class="panels">
        <div class="panel">
            <dt>Budget</dt>
            <dd>
                <span class="count">@Model.Research.Holdout.Count</span>
                <span class="over">@Model.Research.Holdout.Against</span>
                @if (Model.Research.Holdout.FirstSession is string first)
                {
                    <span class="over">the schedule is computed from the earliest session the
                          evidence store holds, which is @first</span>
                }
            </dd>
        </div>
    </dl>

    @if (Model.Research.Holdout.EmptyBecause is string emptyBecause)
    {
        @* An empty register reports why it is empty. Four causes and they are four different
           facts: no session recorded, no quarter matured, every matured window spent, and a
           quarter matured that nothing wrote down. All four hold nought available, and for the
           first months of a lab's life the second and the fourth hold the same noughts on every
           other figure too. *@
        <p class="@(Model.Research.Holdout.ShortOfAWindow ? "down" : "muted")">
            <b>No window is available to spend.</b> @emptyBecause.
        </p>

        @if (Model.Research.Holdout.ShortOfAWindow)
        {
            <p class="down">
                Missing from the register: @string.Join(", ", Model.Research.Holdout.Missing).
                This is a defect rather than a state. The registry records a window the day its
                quarter completes and nothing has recorded these.
            </p>
        }
        else if (Model.Research.Holdout.Exhausted)
        {
            <p class="warns">
                <b>This is a designed dead end rather than a fault.</b> No further pack-version
                decision can be made by replay, and the remaining channel is the forward hit rate.
            </p>
        }
    }

    @if (Model.Research.Holdout.Windows.Count == 0)
    {
        <p class="muted">The register holds no window, which the sentence above accounts for.</p>
    }
    else
    {
        <table class="ledger windows">
            <tr>
                <th>#</th><th>Window</th><th>Quarter</th><th>Matures</th>
                <th>Spent on</th><th>Outcome</th>
            </tr>
            @foreach (WindowView window in Model.Research.Holdout.Windows)
            {
                <tr class="@(window.Available ? null : "resolved")">
                    <td>@window.Ordinal</td>
                    <td>@window.WindowId</td>
                    <td>@window.Start to @window.End</td>
                    <td>@window.MaturesOn</td>
                    <td>@(window.SpentOn ?? "available")</td>
                    <td>@(window.Outcome ?? string.Empty)</td>
                </tr>
            }
        </table>
    }

    <p class="muted">
        <b>Replay is free, and free tests are how you overfit.</b> Sort the same cards forty ways
        and pick the best and you have fitted to those cards. The budget makes the cost explicit and
        finite, which is why a spent window is recorded here with what it was spent on and what came
        of it rather than only that it was spent.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="ledger twins">
    <h2>Twin pairs</h2>
    @*
        Setups that looked the same on every recorded signal and ended somewhere else, which is
        what the signal-request channel is fed from.

        The panel showed an arrival note until 6.3 and now shows a reading. What it must never
        show is a bare nought: the metric standardises each signal over the trailing 250 setups
        and the store holds a fraction of that, so "no twins" and "no window to look in" are two
        different states and the count of setups the window actually held is what tells them
        apart. Every side reports that count whether or not it found a pair.
    *@
    <p class="panel-note">
        A pair qualifies where the two setups sit closer than
        <b>@(Model.Research.Twins.MaximumDistance ?? "-")</b> after standardising and their ten-day
        outcomes differ by more than <b>@(Model.Research.Twins.MinimumGapPoints ?? "-")</b> points.
        Standardised over the trailing <b>@Model.Research.Twins.WindowWanted</b> setups of that side.
        The two sides are read apart and never added.
    </p>

    @if (!Model.Research.Twins.HasReading)
    {
        <div class="empty-state">
            <p><b>No reading.</b> @(Model.Research.Twins.Absent ?? "the finder has not run.")</p>
        </div>
    }
    else
    {
        foreach (var side in Model.Research.Twins.Sides)
        {
            <h3>@side.Direction</h3>
            <p class="population">
                Window held <b>@side.WindowSetups</b> of @side.WindowWanted setups
                @if (side.WindowShortBy > 0)
                {
                    <text>, short by @side.WindowShortBy</text>
                }
                &nbsp;·&nbsp; @side.SignalsCompared signal(s) compared
                &nbsp;·&nbsp; @side.CandidatePairs candidate pair(s)
                &nbsp;·&nbsp; read for @side.AsOf
            </p>

            @if (side.PairsFound == 0)
            {
                <div class="empty-state">
                    <p><b>@side.PairsFound twin pairs</b> over a window of @side.WindowSetups.
                       @side.EmptyBecause</p>
                </div>
            }
            else
            {
                <table class="pairs">
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th>Pair</th><th>Distance</th><th>Gap, points</th>
                            <th>Left outcome</th><th>Right outcome</th><th>Computed over</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                    @foreach (var pair in side.Pairs)
                    {
                        <tr>
                            <td><a href="/setup/@pair.LeftSetupId">@pair.LeftSetupId</a>
                                and <a href="/setup/@pair.RightSetupId">@pair.RightSetupId</a></td>
                            <td>@pair.Distance</td>
                            <td>@pair.GapPoints</td>
                            <td>@pair.LeftOutcome</td>
                            <td>@pair.RightOutcome</td>
                            <td>@pair.SignalsCompared signal(s), @pair.WindowSetups setup(s)</td>
                        </tr>
                    }
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            }
        }
    }

    <p class="panel-note">
        The question a pair is put to the model as is not "predict which one wins", which it
        cannot do. It is: these look identical in everything I record and did opposite things,
        what would you want to see? The model generates candidates to test and does not make
        the call.
    </p>
</section>
